  "description": "NcCache is a C# library for caching file data and objects using content-addressable storage. \n            It is designed for high concurrency and low overhead, utilizing striped reader-writer locks, background worker threads (Lanes), \n            and reference-counted eviction.\n\n            The engine consists of three main layers:\n            - ContentCache: A content-addressable data store mapping 128-bit hashes to byte arrays.\n            - FileStreamCache: A file caching layer that detects file modifications and provides fast-path lookups.\n            - ObjectCache[T]: A generic object cache with generation tracking and asynchronous request processing.\n\n            All state is managed by the `NcCacheEngine`, which orchestrates background threads to process cache requests, \n            evict expired blobs, and detect file changes without blocking the main application.",
  "id": "NcCache",
